---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About | My Static Site" description="Learn more about this site and the person behind it.">
  <article class="about-content">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      This is a simple static site built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a>.
      It demonstrates how to create a fast, accessible website using reusable
      layouts and components with plain CSS styling.
    </p>

    <h2>About Me</h2>
    <p>
      Replace this section with information about yourself or your team.
      You might include your background, interests, skills, or what you are
      working on.
    </p>

    <h2>About This Site</h2>
    <p>
      This starter is designed for beginners learning Astro. It includes:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>A shared layout with navigation and footer</li>
      <li>Reusable components (Hero, Card)</li>
      <li>Responsive design with plain CSS</li>
      <li>SEO basics (meta tags, sitemap, canonical URLs)</li>
      <li>Accessible keyboard navigation with visible focus indicators</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-content {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
